'''Stealth''' is a [[stat]] that makes it more difficult for monsters to see the character from far away. A character with increased stealth can get closer to monsters without them noticing.

==Mechanics==
Stealth reduces the range at which a monster will aggro a target. If a monster would detect a target within its visibility range that has reduced visibility, the range is checked again with reduced visibility applied.<ref name="ReducedVisibilityEffect"/>

Stealth's formula can be calculated by r = 100 / (100+n), where r = the percentage of default aggro radius and n = the total #% increased Stealth.

The maximum achievable #% increased Stealth currently achievable is 360% (using all sources below with two {{il|Ichimonji}}s for 20% increased buff effect). This calculates to ~78% reduction in enemy aggro radius.

It may have uses in situations where players want to avoid getting hit, such as [[Sanctum]] or [[Trial of the Ancestors]].

==Sources==
* {{il|Phase Run}}
* {{sl|Aspect of the Cat}} (Cat's Stealth only)
* {{sl|id=ShadeForm}} buff from [[Shroud of the Lightless]], {{il|Replica Eternity Shroud}}, or {{il|Omen of Death's Door}}
* {{c|mod|50% increased Stealth if you've Hit With a Claw Recently}} [[Claw Mastery]]

==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.12.0|
* Removed the concept 'Reduced Visibility to Enemies' and replaced it with 'Stealth'. Increasing your Stealth reduces the radius at which enemies will notice you. 100% increased Stealth cuts that radius in half, and 200% increased Stealth cuts that radius by two thirds. You can, therefore, no longer become entirely invisible to enemies.
}}
{{Version history table end}}

